riters for game of  thrones  i'm sure some of you have been wondering  if ryan condell is the right fit for  house of the dragon some of you might be  wondering if he even knows anything  about a song of ice and fire well that  answer is yes it seems like he knows a  lot more than the game of thrones  writers did david and dan were fans of a  song of ice and fire whereas it sounds  like ryan is a student of a song of ice  and fire there is a very big difference  i think ryan also has one big advantage  over david and dan house of the dragon  already has an ending george rr martin  laid out all the groundwork for house of  the dragons ending many years ago now i  really want you to hear what else ryan  said during the interview because i  think it says a lot about who he is as a  writer  you know we had done an uh  a round of development  if you go back  when it was clear that the game of  thrones was ending that dave and dan  wanted to end it after seven seasons or  something  hbo started looking to develop other  other shows  and um  the two that i pitched were dancing to  dragon which became  uh house of dragon and uh  the duncan egg thing  but there were a number of other shows  that were developed at that time  most of them put together by writers  that hbo hired  uh  who had never read my books  and who i guess had watched the show and  they were doing and when we were getting  into this i didn't want that anymore i  obviously none of those shows ultimately  got on the air i thought you know i want  people if they're going to be working in  my world i want them to actually have  read my books and i liked ryan's work  and i knew they knew the world he had  read the books so  once again in that bar at the four  seasons uh yeah where it all uh started  there  how tell me about how you guys met a  little bit because i think our audience  would actually really enjoy this i'm a  super fan and i i found the books  at this point over 20 years ago  and uh i love them i 